(6162715, 908305, 9821, '<td valign="top">nice finish, robert</td>', 'nice finish, robert', '2010-09-15 10:30:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(6162761, 908009, 33361, '<td valign="top">Hey Tori!! It''s Roseann (I met you and your dad in Ft. Worth).. glad to see you entered one of the challenges. I gave you a 7 and I think this one is great! : )</td>', 'Hey Tori!! It''s Roseann (I met you and your dad in Ft. Worth).. glad to see you entered one of the challenges. I gave you a 7 and I think this one is great! : )', '2010-09-15 11:13:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(6162782, 907925, 108580, '<td valign="top">I must say it''s nice to get a few comments, even from Sarampo, albeit harsh. I was torn over submitting tight cropped or subject free shots.<br/>Maybe I should have submitted this.<br/><img alt="'' . substr(''//farm5.static.flickr.com/4112/4986906822_e9d061e223_m.jpg'', strrpos(''//farm5.static.flickr.com/4112/4986906822_e9d061e223_m.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//farm5.static.flickr.com/4112/4986906822_e9d061e223_m.jpg"/> <br/>or this<br/><img alt="'' . substr(''//farm5.static.flickr.com/4148/4986305371_d65f60cf1b_m.jpg'', strrpos(''//farm5.static.flickr.com/4148/4986305371_d65f60cf1b_m.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//farm5.static.flickr.com/4148/4986305371_d65f60cf1b_m.jpg"/> <br/>and then gotten a "Subjects are too far away" comments :)</td>', 'I must say it''s nice to get a few comments, even from Sarampo, albeit harsh. I was torn over submitting tight cropped or subject free shots.Maybe I should have submitted this. or this and then gotten a "Subjects are too far away" comments :)', '2010-09-15 11:28:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(6162792, 907925, 105457, '<td valign="top">Hi Harvey!<br/> <br/>Not meant to be rude, sorry :-S Sometimes I comment too quickly.<br/>I do think both your outtakes are better than the submitted version, the first one has a great leading line, with help from the smoke trail, and the other has very good composition. I''m also sometimes torn between which version to choose, but as I know that I''ll never find out how the outtake would do, I tend not to worry much ;-)</td>', 'Hi Harvey! Not meant to be rude, sorry :-S Sometimes I comment too quickly.I do think both your outtakes are better than the submitted version, the first one has a great leading line, with help from the smoke trail, and the other has very good composition. I''m also sometimes torn between which version to choose, but as I know that I''ll never find out how the outtake would do, I tend not to worry much ;-)', '2010-09-15 11:38:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(6162798, 907925, 108580, '<td valign="top">Hi J, no offense taken. I appreciate ALL comments, "sugar coated" or "harsh". They are all useful to me! It was a love it/hate it shot judging by the &lt;5 and &gt;5 votes.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-09-15 10:47:42.</i></td>', 'Hi J, no offense taken. I appreciate ALL comments, "sugar coated" or "harsh". They are all useful to me! It was a love it/hate it shot judging by the <5 and >5 votes.', '2010-09-15 11:47:02.000000', '2010-09-15 11:47:42.000000', 0),
(6162832, 908245, 10785, '<td valign="top">This is just in response to your request for comments in the forums...<br/> <br/>I voted a 4 on this. For me it met the challenge well. I liked the composition well enough and the fact that the challenge subject was a nice pop of color. <br/> <br/>What I found to be lacking in the photo was the background. There is something funky with the leaves and stuff not really looking blurred through the shallow depth of field, but by some other wierd means. Also it had some high noise for the time of day it was taken. I would have liked to see this sharper and crisper.<br/> <br/>Also be careful with the ruleset. I believe dodging and burning is illegal under basic rules as it is considered spot editing. I could be wrong though.</td>', 'This is just in response to your request for comments in the forums... I voted a 4 on this. For me it met the challenge well. I liked the composition well enough and the fact that the challenge subject was a nice pop of color.  What I found to be lacking in the photo was the background. There is something funky with the leaves and stuff not really looking blurred through the shallow depth of field, but by some other wierd means. Also it had some high noise for the time of day it was taken. I would have liked to see this sharper and crisper. Also be careful with the ruleset. I believe dodging and burning is illegal under basic rules as it is considered spot editing. I could be wrong though.', '2010-09-15 12:19:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(6162836, 908245, 83313, '<td valign="top">Copy of my response in the forum:<br/> <br/>I gave this a 5, but I tend to be a generous voter, so I figured others would slam it and they did. Here are what I see as the problems that brought it down:<br/>-Noisy, or grainy image. Weird pattern is visible in the background foliage. Perhaps an extreme crop?<br/>-objects on the left edge of the frame that don''t add anything to the scene.<br/>-Subject slightly off center, but not enough to seem intentionally composed that way.<br/>-Just an overall lack of clarity.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-09-15 11:21:27.</i></td>', 'Copy of my response in the forum: I gave this a 5, but I tend to be a generous voter, so I figured others would slam it and they did. Here are what I see as the problems that brought it down:-Noisy, or grainy image. Weird pattern is visible in the background foliage. Perhaps an extreme crop?-objects on the left edge of the frame that don''t add anything to the scene.-Subject slightly off center, but not enough to seem intentionally composed that way.-Just an overall lack of clarity.', '2010-09-15 12:21:18.000000', '2010-09-15 12:21:27.000000', 0),
