(6171596, 908284, 103547, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by pichichib:</b></div><hr/><i> Great picture, congrats. I just have one question how did you manage to get the background not to be blurry with that aperture f4. Is it the type of lens. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>The thing is that that roof structure was alredy really high.  F4 was then enough to cover the focus range between visible objects.</td>', 'Originally posted by pichichib: Great picture, congrats. I just have one question how did you manage to get the background not to be blurry with that aperture f4. Is it the type of lens.   The thing is that that roof structure was alredy really high.  F4 was then enough to cover the focus range between visible objects.', '2010-09-25 12:43:50.000000', NULL, 0),
